       these checks fails, sscchheedd__sseettaattttrr(2) fails with the error EEIINNVVAALL.

       The  CBS  guarantees  non‐interference  between  tasks,  by  throttling
       threads that attempt to over‐run their specified Runtime.

       To ensure deadline scheduling guarantees, the kernel must prevent situ‐
       ations where the set of SSCCHHEEDD__DDEEAADDLLIINNEE threads is not feasible (schedu‐
       lable)  within  the given constraints.  The kernel thus performs an ad‐
